ame>TAMAI KATSUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOJI SHINGO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANO MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMAI, KATSUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOJI, SHINGO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANO, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A novel selenocysteine insertion sequence (SECIS). This SECIS, which consists of a small number of bases of less than 360b, ensures the insertion of selenocysteine into a translational region. It is useful in expressing selenoproteins having selenocysteine as an essential constituting amino acid such as thioredoxin reductase.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une nouvelle séquence d'insertion de sélénocystéine (SECIS). Cette nouvelle séquence SECIS, composée d'un petit nombre de bases de moins de 360b, assure l'insertion de la sélénocystéine dans une région de traduction. Il est en effet utile d'exprimer des sélénoprotéines renfermant la sélénocystéine comme aminoacide constituant essentiel, par exemple la thiorédoxine réductase.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agre